Voice Pilot Constitution and Bilateral Transcription Architecture
The conversational intelligence layer—embodied in ⁠src/App.tsx⁠, ⁠src/components/VoiceCard.tsx⁠, and ⁠server.ts⁠—is architected around a bilateral transcription and tool-calling paradigm. While the backend status endpoint (⁠/api/gemini/status⁠) is wired to verify credentials for ⁠gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025⁠ and ⁠gemini-3-flash-preview⁠, the behavioral rules implemented in the client state machine strictly codify the studio's voice pilot instructions (⁠01 KB handoff⁠ and ⁠Master Instruction v2⁠).
Arrival Authentication and Audience Awareness Protocol
The voice pilot's initialization sequence is deterministic and stripped of conversational bloat. Requirement 4 in ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ dictates that upon completing or bypassing the 8-second boot sequence, ⁠Cerebro⁠ emits strictly two lines and nothing else: at timestamp ⁠00:00⁠ (⁠id: 'init-1'⁠, ⁠toolCalled: 'arrival_greet'⁠), the pilot states ⁠"Welcome back, sir."⁠, followed immediately at ⁠00:01⁠ (⁠id: 'init-2'⁠, ⁠toolCalled: 'arrival_greet'⁠) by ⁠"Anyone with you?"⁠.
This second prompt directly drives the Audience Awareness Lock (⁠AudienceLevel⁠: ⁠'owner' | 'partner' | 'public'⁠), which defaults to ⁠'owner'⁠ while displaying a translucent top-center prompt banner (⁠Cerebro: "Anyone with you?"⁠) with one-tap selectors for ⁠Owner only⁠, ⁠Partner / Assistant⁠, and ⁠Public⁠. In tandem with the numeric Owner Lock Keypad (⁠ownerUnlocked⁠), this privacy state dynamically filters the 3D scene graph and station panels so that sensitive records—such as ⁠SAMPLE Project 02 (Owner Only)⁠, ⁠tsk-04⁠ (⁠Owner-only contract addendum review⁠), ⁠SAMPLE_NOJARA_HQ_Master_Governance.pdf⁠, and personnel buyout/retainer clauses (⁠contractNoteOwnerOnly⁠)—remain completely invisible in both the 3D label projection layer and the HTML DOM until both ⁠audience === 'owner'⁠ and ⁠ownerUnlocked === true⁠ are satisfied.
Silent Tool Execution vs. Queued Vocalization
A defining architectural characteristic of the CEREBRO voice specification is the separation of kinetic action from verbal feedback. In conventional voice interfaces, every command triggers a redundant verbal confirmation, which introduces cognitive friction during rapid spatial navigation. Requirement 5 in ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ explicitly prohibits chatty acknowledgments (⁠"locked on"⁠ or ⁠"ok — Travelled to..."⁠) and enforces a calm, unhurried operational demeanor. When the operator issues any navigation, sphere-switching, camera-rig, orbital-spin, background-mode, or panel-closing command (⁠switch_sphere⁠, ⁠navigate_to⁠, ⁠open_station⁠, ⁠open_panel⁠, ⁠open_item⁠, ⁠focus_project⁠, ⁠open_dimension⁠, ⁠open_subdomain⁠, ⁠open_chapter⁠, ⁠camera⁠, ⁠auto_orbit⁠, ⁠play_media⁠, ⁠pause_media⁠, ⁠set_volume⁠, ⁠close_panel⁠, ⁠set_background⁠, ⁠set_audience⁠, or ⁠get_page_state⁠), ⁠executeTool⁠ mutates the React state and Three.js camera targets silently without pushing any string to the speech queue.
Conversely, vocalization (⁠voiceState = 'Speaking'⁠) and 3D floating bubble projection (⁠floatingBubbleText⁠) are invoked via ⁠speakLine(text, toolName)⁠ exclusively under five bounded conditions: the two-part arrival greeting (⁠arrival_greet⁠); sequential stop narrations during the 6-stop guided tour (⁠tour_stop_1⁠ through ⁠tour_stop_6⁠); interruption notifications when manual touch, pointer drag, wheel zoom, or voice pauses an active tour (⁠"Tour paused."⁠ via ⁠pause_tour⁠); direct analytical queries (⁠get_projects⁠, ⁠get_project⁠, ⁠get_briefing⁠, ⁠get_raci⁠, ⁠search_files⁠, ⁠log_feedback⁠, and ⁠get_live_feed⁠); and task synthesis prompts triggered from the Compose pocket (⁠"Make this a task?"⁠ via ⁠compose_analyse⁠).
Speech Queue Cadence and Caption Decay Mechanics
When ⁠speakLine(text, toolName)⁠ is invoked, the system appends a structured ⁠TranscriptEntry⁠ (⁠id⁠, ⁠speaker: 'Cerebro'⁠, ⁠text⁠, ⁠toolCalled⁠, ⁠timestamp⁠) to the bilateral transcription state and enqueues ⁠text⁠ into ⁠narrationQueueRef.current⁠. The queue processor (⁠processQueue⁠) enforces a two-stage temporal lifecycle:
Each queued line holds the ⁠'Speaking'⁠ state for ⁠1,600 ms⁠ before advancing to the next item. Once the queue is exhausted, ⁠voiceState⁠ reverts to ⁠'Listening'⁠, and ⁠captionTimerRef⁠ initiates a ⁠2,400 ms⁠ silence countdown after which ⁠liveCaption⁠ is cleared to ⁠null⁠.
