Technical Synthesis and Actionable Engineering Recommendations
A cross-module static analysis of the ⁠cerebro-+-cde.zip⁠ build surfaces three high-priority engineering actions required to transition the workspace from its current simulated preview state to a zero-error production deployment. First, schema-to-prop drift inside ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ must be reconciled prior to live voice deployment. While the child components (⁠DualSphereCanvas.tsx⁠, ⁠StationPanels.tsx⁠, ⁠VoiceCard.tsx⁠, and ⁠OwnerLockKeypad.tsx⁠) and data definitions (⁠cerebroData.ts⁠) implement the updated Master Instruction v2 interfaces, ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ retains legacy v1 prop names (⁠hasOpenHybridPanel⁠ instead of ⁠hasOpen3DPanel⁠, ⁠onSelectProjectSun⁠ instead of ⁠onSelectProject⁠, ⁠onFileSearchChange⁠ instead of ⁠onChangeFileSearch⁠, and ⁠onInvokeTool⁠ instead of ⁠onExecuteToolDirect⁠) and references ⁠proj.sunPosition⁠ instead of ⁠proj.sunPositionHq⁠ and ⁠proj.sunPositionCde⁠. Aligning these bindings in ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ and eliminating the duplicate ⁠buildLiquidGlassGalaxySphere(CEREBRO_CENTER, colCobalt)⁠ invocation in ⁠DualSphereCanvas.tsx⁠ (lines 410–414) restores clean TypeScript compilation (⁠tsc --noEmit⁠) and reclaims ⁠3,200⁠ redundant GPU vertices.
Second, stripped Arabic string literals inside ⁠handleExecuteCommand⁠ in ⁠src/App.tsx⁠ should be restored and supplemented with direct client-tool JSON bindings. Because several Arabic/Masri string literals inside ⁠handleExecuteCommand⁠ were reduced to single space characters (⁠' '⁠) during archive serialization, substring checks such as ⁠lower.includes(' ')⁠ inadvertently match any multi-word English command containing a space and prematurely trigger ⁠stop_tour⁠. Replacing those blank substring checks with explicit UTF-8 Arabic keywords and binding the 25 ⁠executeTool⁠ handlers directly as structured ⁠clientTools⁠ for the conversational agent eliminates natural-language routing ambiguity.
Finally, live upstream credentials should be injected to activate bilateral audio streaming and NOJARA HQ register synchronization. Both the Express server (⁠server.ts⁠) and the client UI are engineered for strict data truthfulness, explicitly displaying ⁠GEMINI LIVE: BLOCKED (NEEDS KEY)⁠ and ⁠SAMPLE (Awaiting 07 Project Register)⁠ until valid environment secrets are detected. Provisioning ⁠GEMINI_API_KEY⁠ alongside ⁠NOJARA_HQ_PROJECT_REGISTER_ID⁠ and ⁠NOJARA_HQ_DRIVE_ROOT_ID⁠ transitions the CEREBRO + CDE workspace from its ⁠SIMULATED⁠ and ⁠SAMPLE⁠ fallback states into full bilateral voice pilotage and live studio register telemetry.